    {
      "id": 107062,
      "name": "MigrantP",
      "username": "MigrantP",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-06-25T20:23:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Multiple targets are most likely to be sequential \"choose a target\" steps, because the available targets can change in between damage dealing. It would also be more difficult to show the calculations/effects for many targets at once.</p><p>If you're damaging all targets, or all targets of a certain class (e.g. all non-hero targets), then you're essentially choosing the order in which they will be damaged. In that case, there will be an \"I don't care\" button (or similar) that just does all the damage in whatever order. Most of the time that's ok, but some times you'll want to carefully choose the order.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:37:09.892Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
