      "id": 107066,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-06-27T18:43:47.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MigrantP\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/48/1921_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MigrantP:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For sure, and of course Absolute Zero often likes to target himself. That's why the option is available. You can do anything in the digital version that you can in the table top game =)Though as a side note, I don't think that combo works exactly, since&nbsp;Driving Mantis only works for 2 or less damage. If you have Dual Crowbars and Harmony in play, you're doing 3 damage minimum. Unless you have a point of damage reduction from some other effect.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Actually, as per the newest ruling on Fortitude/Superhuman Durability, you could possibly trigger Mantis before resolving the +damage. Similar to how you can choose whether or not to trigger Superhuman Durability before or after Fortitude depending on the situation. I'm sure Ronway will chime in if I'm mistaken here.</p>\n<p>This is not something I have been able to test out in the Mega Computer yet. Maybe I should try and do that.</p>",
